{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Bayes' Theorem Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Bayes theorem function"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def bayes(prior, likelihood, false_positive_rate):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    evidence = likelihood * prior + false_positive_rate * (1 - prior)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    posterior = likelihood * prior / evidence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return posterior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result = bayes(prior=0.0001, likelihood=0.99, false_positive_rate=0.01)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"P(sick|positive) = {result:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Naive Bayes classifier"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from collections import defaultdict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class NaiveBayes:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, smoothing=1.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.smoothing = smoothing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.class_counts = defaultdict(int)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.word_counts = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(int))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.class_word_totals = defaultdict(int)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.vocab = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def train(self, documents, labels):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for doc, label in zip(documents, labels):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.class_counts[label] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            words = doc.lower().split()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for word in words:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.word_counts[label][word] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.class_word_totals[label] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                self.vocab.add(word)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, document):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        words = document.lower().split()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_docs = sum(self.class_counts.values())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        vocab_size = len(self.vocab)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        best_class = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        best_score = float(\"-inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for cls in self.class_counts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            score = math.log(self.class_counts[cls] / total_docs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for word in words:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                count = self.word_counts[cls].get(word, 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                total = self.class_word_totals[cls]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                score += math.log((count + self.smoothing) / (total + self.smoothing * vocab_size))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if score > best_score:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                best_score = score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                best_class = cls"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return best_class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Log probabilities prevent underflow. Multiplying many small probabilities produces numbers too tiny for floating point. Summing log-probabilities is numerically stable and mathematically equivalent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Train on spam data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "train_docs = ["
      ]
    },
